<h1>busy beaver</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
(1) A <a href="turingMachine.html"><em>Turing machine</em></a> with a small number of <a href="state.html"><em>states</em></a> that halts when started with a blank tape, but writes a huge number of non-blanks or takes a huge number of steps.  (2) The problem of finding the maximum number of non-blanks written or steps taken for any Turing machines with a given number of states and symbols.
</p>


<p>
<em>Note:
The problem is well-defined but rapidly becomes impractical to determine for even a small number of states and symbols. This problem is related to the <a href="haltingProblem.html"><em>halting problem</em></a> since one must determine if a machine is looping or eventually halts.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
History, explanation, and links about the <a href="http://grail.cba.csuohio.edu/~somos/bb.html" target="_blank">Busy Beaver Turing Machine</a>. Heiner Marxen's  <a href="http://turbotm.de/~heiner/BB/" target="_blank">currently known busy beaver results</a> page.
</p>

